{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b820-1ca5-73f3-80c2-643ddbe066f7","session_id":"01a1b81d-ccd0-73f3-8dba-319230e0d711","message":{"id":"01a1b8201ca573f380c2643bf618acb4","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"check-fast runs every scripts/check-*.mjs without args — including check-write-scope? Without --base/--scope, it only does the manifest check → ok. Good, no git.\n\nSo `check-unused: ok` appears in output. Let me confirm from the earlier full output (truncated). I'll trust it since check-unused is a check-*.mjs and exits 0.\n\nNow let me write acceptance.md.\n\nAlso need to double check: the note says \"Your acceptance.md has 66 code fences but ZERO headings of the form '## AC-xxx'\". So keep fenced code blocks minimal or none. I'll use only `- 命令:` lines. Maybe keep a small fenced block for the exported output expectation in A-10? Better avoid fences entirely to keep extraction clean (fences don't hurt, but simpler).\n\nNow writing. Intro should keep baseline info and the contract note. Keep concise.\n\nLet me now write each command fully with absolute base:\n\nB = C:/git/dsh-CLIWorker/.collab/worktrees/007\n\nFull command list:\n\nAC-020 A-01:\n`$o = & node C:/.../scripts/run-tests.mjs --ac AC-020 2>&1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; if (-not ($o -match 'fail 0')) { exit 1 }; if (-not ($o -match 'filtered 3 files')) { exit 1 }; Write-Output \"AC-020 OK\"`\n\nAC-020 A-02:\n`node -e \"import('file:///C:/.../lib/select.mjs').then(({selectModels})=>{const c={providers:{claude:{cli:'claude',readonly:true}},models:{q:{provider:'claude',id:'q',level:'Quick',identity:'verified'}}};const r=selectModels(c,{level:'Quick'},{status:{claude:{state:'callable'}}});const h=r.models[0];if(!h||('cli' in h)!==false||('call' in h)!==true||JSON.stringify(h.call)!==JSON.stringify(r.calls[0]))process.exit(1)})\"; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; Write-Output \"AC-020 OK\"`\n\nHmm: `!` in PS double-quoted strings — is `!` special? No. But wait, PowerShell 5.1 in double-quoted strings: `$` is special, backtick special, `\"` ends. `!` fine.\n\nBut `!==` is fine.\n\nHmm, one thing: `('cli' in h)` — the `'` quotes inside a double-quoted PS string are literal. Good.\n\nAC-020 A-03 similarly.\n\nAC-020 A-04: uses `new Set(...)`. Fine.\n\nWait, A-04's JS: `out.add(seen.length+'/'+new Set(seen).size)` then check out.size===1 && out.has('8/8'). Good.\n\nAC-020 A-05:\n`$o = & node --test C:/.../a5-dup-call.test.mjs C:/.../a5-forecast-x3.test.mjs 2>&1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; if (-not ($o -match 'pass 4')) { exit 1 }; if (-not ($o -match 'fail 0')) { exit 1 }; Write-Output \"AC-020 OK\"`\n\nAC-020 A-06:\n`$o = & git -C C:/... diff f6f6057 -- test/characterization/defects.json; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; if (\"$o\".Trim().Length -ne 0) { exit 1 }; Write-Output \"AC-020 OK\"`\n\nHmm: `& git -C path diff ...` — PowerShell parses fine.\n\nAC-020 A-07 (select.test unchanged + pass 6):\n`$o = & node --test C:/.../test/unit/select.test.mjs 2>&1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; if (-not ($o -match 'pass 6')) { exit 1 }; if (-not ($o -match 'fail 0')) { exit 1 }; $d = & git -C C:/... diff f6f6057 -- test/unit/select.test.mjs; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; if (\"$d\".Trim().Length -ne 0) { exit 1 }; Write-Output \"AC-020 OK\"`\n\nAC-021 A-08: run-tests AC-021 filtered 1 files.\nAC-021 A-09: golden heavy. The JS is long. Node -e with the whole thing.\n\nLet me rewrite A-08's JS for absolute paths: it imports './lib/select.mjs', './lib/forecast.mjs', and reads 'contracts/golden/quota-shapes.json' — must be absolute.\n\n`import('file:///C:/.../lib/select.mjs')`, `import('file:///C:/.../lib/forecast.mjs')`, `fs.readFileSync('C:/.../contracts/golden/quota-shapes.json','utf8')`.\n\nAssertions: got === want (sorted), want.length>=5, h.rejected.length===want.length, n.rejected.length===0, l.rejected.length===0.\n\nHmm: `h.rejected.length===want.length` assumes only Heavy-rejection entries. Let me verify with a run later.\n\nAC-021 A-10: exports list + heavyRejection behavior:\n`import('file:///.../lib/select-draft.mjs')` then checks:\n- Object.keys(m).sort().join(',') === 'HANDLE_SCHEMA,HEAVY_REJECT_RISKS,SELECTION_SCHEMA,draftHandle,draftSelection,heavyRejection'\n- heavyRejection returns reason for 3 risks, null for ok/unknown\n- null for Normal/Light.\n\nAC-021 A-11: a1-quota unchanged via git diff.\n\nAC-022 A-12: run-tests AC-022 filtered 2 files.\nAC-022 A-13: check-unused default ok (files=N, N>0): \n`$o = & node C:/.../check-unused.mjs 2>&1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }; if (-not (\"$o\" -match '^check-unused: ok \\(files=[1-9][0-9]*\\)$')) { exit 1 }; Write-Output \"AC-022 OK\"`\nSince output single line + newline; \"$o\" is the string; `-match` with ^...$ may fail due to trailing newline. Use `\"$o\".Trim() -match '^check-unused: ok \\(files=[1-9][0-9]*\\)$'`. Trim handles it.\n\nAC-022 A-14: json 8 items + exit 1.\nAC-022 A-15: clean files=1.\nAC-022 A-16: usage errors exit 2.\nAC-022 A-17: a5-unused pass 2 + isObject count 0.\nAC-022 A-18: check-unused self files=1.\nAC-022 A-19: validate.mjs numstat + typeOf absent.\nAC-022 A-20: check-defects ok.\nAC-022 A-21: traceability covered=22 planned=52.\nAC-022 A-22: seams files=21 or 22.\nAC-022 A-23: no-collab ok; golden-frozen 14 files. Could combine — but separate sections better.\nAC-022 A-24: write scope.\nAC-022 A-25: check-fast.\nAC-022 A-26: npm test.\nAC-022 A-27: zero deps + package.json unchanged.\n\nHmm, \"npm test\" — from TEMP with `npm --prefix`. Also `git diff --stat -- package.json package-lock.json` no output.\n\nThat's a lot of sections (27). Fine.\n\nWait: is it OK that AC-022 has 15 sections? Rule 4: \"Cover each AC you own with its own section.\" Multiple sections per AC is fine.\n\nHmm, but maybe the runner expects exactly one section per AC? \"Every check MUST be: ## AC-020 Short title ...\" and \"Cover each AC you own with its own section.\" With multiple, the runner runs each and requires \"AC-022 